[Desktop Entry]
# Handles claude-cli:// deep links. Claude Code installs this entry itself, in
# ~/.local/share/applications; this is a repo-managed replacement whose only
# difference is Exec, which goes through bin/claude-env instead of calling the
# binary directly.
#
# Why: a .desktop entry is launched by the desktop environment, not by a shell,
# so it never sources ~/env and never gets MEM0_API_KEY. Claude Code then runs
# with mem0 silently disabled. claude-env sources ~/.config/env-secrets.zsh
# first and execs the real binary -- see that script for the full story.
#
# This one is RENDERED by init/links.zsh, not symlinked: the placeholder in
# Exec is replaced with the repo's real path (which is why no other line may
# contain it). A .desktop Exec is not run through a shell, so it cannot
# expand $HOME -- and the two machines have different usernames, so the literal
# path cannot live in the repo either. Field codes (%u) must stay outside
# quotes and outside any `sh -c`, which is why this is not solved with a
# wrapper command; the launcher then substitutes nothing and Claude Code opens
# with no URI.
#
# Claude Code may rewrite its own copy on update. Re-running init restores this
# version; if deep links start losing mem0, diff ~/.local/share/applications/
# claude-code-url-handler.desktop against this file.
Name=Claude Code URL Handler
Comment=Handle claude-cli:// deep links for Claude Code
Exec=@ENV_DIR@/bin/claude-env --handle-uri %u
Type=Application
NoDisplay=true
MimeType=x-scheme-handler/claude-cli;
